## Context

Tracker [[1703]], document 3. Scattered today over [[0725]] (M3a stopping
rule, authority frame), [[1180]], [[1184]], [[1140]], [[1141]], the Collection
section of `data/jetp/README.md`, `docs/jetp-country-source-policy.md`,
`docs/jetp-scout-brief.md` and the `jetp-research` skill. M3a publishes a
discovery cutoff, a recall estimate and a list of unreachable sources; they
need a stated protocol to be citable.

## Author constraints (2026-09-30, interactive)

- "What we are working towards is a complete system specification. The idea
  is to write it explicit and review the heck out of it before we launch
  extraction."
- "We want something that works first, then M4 will polish."
- "Pragmatic programmer, results-oriented over theoretical purity."
- Conceptual documents name no storage and no presentation (rule set for
  `docs/jetp-fusion.md`, ticket 1701).

So every rule in a spec document carries the milestone that needs it (M2,
M3a, M3b, M4, or later). The M2 and M3 slice is the minimum that produces
correct, traceable results; everything else is tagged M4 or later and is not
built before it.

## Exit criteria

- [ ] `docs/jetp-collection.md`, conceptual (no storage, no presentation), covers the authority frame, channel classes and their pedigree, rounds and the stopping rule, recall estimation with a known-item list, access limits and terms of use, living documents and series
- [ ] Every rule carries its milestone; the M3a slice is the minimum that yields a citable recall estimate
- [ ] The scattered sources above point to it or are reduced to what is operational
